    "title": "Where to watch the Guardians vs Mariners game tonight",
    "text": "March 27, 2026, 3:43 p.m. ETYou can't win 'em all if you don't win the first one.Well, the Cleveland Guardians delivered in the opening game of the 2026 MLB season, defeating the Seattle Mariners 6-4 in Seattle. It was a coming-out party for rookie outfielder Chase DeLauter, who went 3-for-5 and launched two home runs in the win.Opening Day starter Tanner Bibee allowed three home runs of his own, but all three were solo shots for the Mariners, and that's all they'd muster offensively off the righty. Bibee went five innings allowing four hits, three runs and two walks while striking out seven in a steady season debut before leaving with shoulder inflammation.Cleveland's bullpen allowed just one additional run in four innings of work in the win.Fans will need alternative viewing means to watch Game 2 of the 2026 season, though, as the series against the M's continues.Here's how to tune in.How to watch Guardians vs Mariners game Friday, March 27The second game of the opening series against the Mariners will be streaming exclusively on Apple TV.First pitch is scheduled for 9:40 p.m. ET.Who are the projected starters in Game 2 between the Guardians and Mariners?On the bump for the Guardians following Bibee will be right-hander Gavin Williams.The 6-foot-6, 26-year-old started 31 games for Cleveland a season ago. He finished with a 12-5 record to accompany a 3.06 ERA. He struck out 173 batters in 167.2 innings, but often had trouble with control. He walked a league-high 83 hitters a season ago, so he'll look to improve his command to build off what he established a season ago in what was otherwise viewed as the best year of his young career.For the Mariners, George Kirby will take the mound for his first start of 2026. Kirby is the opposite end of the coin when compared to Williams, as he walked just 29 batters a season ago — which was a career-high. He finished the 2025 campaign with career worst 4.21 ERA to go with a 10-8 record over the course of 23 starts.The Akron Beacon Journal sports department can be contacted via email at bjsports@thebeaconjournal.com.",
